 ## Source generators and compile-time registration
 
 **General rule:** reflection is fine in JIT scenarios, and you can often keep it and annotate it instead (see the DAM section). Use this technique when you *want the reflective surface gone* — for example, a public registration API you do not want to ship with `[RequiresUnreferencedCode]`. The only way to *eliminate* a warning class is to remove the reflection: replace runtime discovery — `Assembly.GetTypes()`, `AppDomain` scanning, `Activator.CreateInstance(Type)`, `type.GetMethod("name")` — with a source generator that emits direct type references at compile time.
 
